{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/904662-sidereals-wfhl-peerless-masters-of-the-martial-arts-throne-shadow-style","id":904662,"title":"[Sidereals:WFHL] Peerless Masters of the Martial Arts: Throne Shadow Style","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Sidereal Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-05-31T19:48:39-07:00","id":904662,"title":"[Sidereals:WFHL] Peerless Masters of the Martial Arts: Throne Shadow Style","content":"Throne Shadow Weapons: This style counts as unarmed attacks the cestus, fighting gauntlet, khatars, pankrator\u2019s cestus, tiger claws, and other such \u2018brawling aides\u2019, as well as improvised weapons. <br /> <br /> Armor: Throne Shadow Style is compatible with any sort of armor<br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://i.imgur.com/e0a5oQh.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:purple\"><b><i>Sifu's Useful Fingers</i></b></span><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 1m; <b>Mins:</b> Martial Arts (Throne Shadow Style) 2, Essence 1<br /> <b>Type:</b> Simple<br /> <b>Keywords:</b> Terrestrial<br /> <b>Duration:</b> Indefinite<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms:</b> None<br /> <br /> Sidereals advise the world; much of their power to act upon the world proceeds from this fact. Disdaining such crude weapons as fighting gauntlets or appropriated bar stools, the martial artist turns others into his instruments\u2014 be they pawns or kings. She may enlighten an individual with five minutes of one-on-one advice and simple-but-profound martial demonstrations. If the target is an unwilling pupil, then the Sidereal may also be required to succeed at a (Manipulation + Martial Arts) action against her target's Resolve. <br /> The beneficiaries of such instruction, known as fingers or shadow fingers, gain a bonus dot in any one of Martial Arts, Brawl, Athletics or Dodge, as chosen by the martial artist. The martial artist may only select an ability in which the student has a rating lower than the Sidereal's Martial Art's rating as well as the Sidereal's rating in the chosen ability. Additionally, the target gains a minor tie of loyalty towards the martial artist; so long as the mote remains committed, nothing can completely remove this loyalty. The martial artist may maintain up to (Essence x2) fingers at once.<br /> <b>Terestrial</b>: The martial artist may only maintain (Essence) fingers at once.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:purple\"><b><i>Lotus Eye Tactics</i></b></span><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 1m; <b>Mins:</b> Martial Arts (Throne Shadow Style) 2, Essence 1<br /> <b>Type:</b> Simple<br /> <b>Keywords:</b> Mastery, Terrestrial<br /> <b>Duration:</b> Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms:</b> None<br /> <br /> Sidereals understand the world; much of their power to act upon the world proceeds from this fact. By studying the subtle movements of an individual, the martial artist comes to understand how versed they are in deadly arts. She rolls (Perception + Martial Arts) against her target's Guile; if she is successful, she learns his highest Martial Arts rating and what style it is in, as well as his Archery, Athletics, Awareness, Brawl, Dodge, Melee, and Thrown ratings.<br /> <b>Mastery</b>: The martial artist may use Lotus Eye Tactics Reflexively when in combat, rather than as a Simple action.<br /> <b>Terrestrial</b>: The martial artist only learns the target's highest Martial Arts rating and what style it is in.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:purple\"><b><i>Lion Mouse Stratagem</i></b></span><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 3m; <b>Mins:</b> Martial Arts (Throne Shadow Style) 3, Essence 1<br /> <b>Type:</b> Simple<br /> <b>Keywords:</b> Mastery<br /> <b>Duration:</b> One Scene<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms:</b> None<br /> <br /> Sidereals deceive the world, presenting themselves as less than what they are; much of their power to act upon the world proceeds from this fact. The martial artist cloaks herself in the humble and unassuming air of the neophyte student, the civil servant, or the hanger-on in the company of legends. She seems uninteresting, increasing her Guile by (Martial Arts /2) as a non-charm bonus when defending against attempts to gauge her nature or the level of her skill. This unassuming mien also makes it easier to dismiss the Sidereal out of hand; anyone who attempts to notice the martial artist when she is concealed suffer a penalty of -(higher of Essence or 2). Both these effects end after the martial artist makes an attack or otherwise draws attention to herself, and may not be resumed during the scene.<br /> <b>Mastery</b>: The martial artist may pay up to (Martial Arts) additional motes when activating Lion Mouse Stratagem; for each additional mote spent, she extends the benefits of the charm to one of her shadow fingers. She may conceal no more than (Martial Arts) fingers at a time in this fashion. If the effect ends for the martial artist, it immediately ends for her fingers as well; if one of her fingers attacks or draws attention to himself, the effect ends for him but not for the martial artist or her fingers. <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:purple\"><b><i>Throne Shadow Form</i></b></span><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 6m; <b>Mins:</b> Martial Arts (Throne Shadow Style) 3, Essence 2<br /> <b>Type:</b> Simple<br /> <b>Keywords:</b> Form<br /> <b>Duration:</b> One Scene<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms:</b> Sifu's Useful Fingers, Lotus Eye Tactics, Lion Mouse Stratagem<br /> <br /> Combining insight, deceit, and the shadow fingers she has accumulated, the Sidereal makes a terrible fist with which to guard all things within destiny\u2019s design. While this Form is active, all shadow fingers within close range of the martial artist may take a reflexive defend other action to guard the martial artist at no cost. Additionally, if her fingers form a battle group, the Sidereal may make a reflexive command action (Exalted p. 209) once per turn on her action, substituting her Martial Arts for her War. Finally, the martial artist and her fingers within Close range may strike dematerialized targets normally, although they gain no special ability to find and target such beings.<br /> <b>Special activation rules</b>: When the Sidereal is within Close range of three or more of their shadow fingers, she may activate Throne Shadow Form reflexively.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:purple\"><b><i>Clear Eyes Defense</i></b></span><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 3m; <b>Mins:</b> Martial Arts (Throne Shadow Style) 5, Essence 2<br /> <b>Type:</b> Reflexive<br /> <b>Keywords:</b> Decisive-only, Counterattack, Mastery, Perilous<br /> <b>Duration:</b> Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms:</b> Throne Shadow Form<br /> <br /> The Sidereals are destiny\u2019s guardians and the eyes of the Exalted. Their vision must not be clouded, and those who would attempt such stratagems must be punished. When the martial artist is targeted by an effect with the Psyche keyword, if the originator of the effect is within Close range, she may make a decisive counterattack against him before the Psyche effect takes hold. If she has not joined battle before invoking this charm, she rolls Join Battle normally to determine her initiative. Clear Eyes Defense does not count as the martial artist's action and cannot be used in response to another counterattack.<br /> <b>Mastery</b>: If the martial artist's counterattack deals at least 1 level of damage, she may spend 1 willpower to ignore the Psyche effect which provoked the counterattack.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:purple\"><b><i>Shadow Lost in Court</i></b></span><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 5m; <b>Mins:</b> Martial Arts (Throne Shadow Style) 4, Essence 2<br /> <b>Type:</b> Supplemental<br /> <b>Keywords:</b> Terrestrial<br /> <b>Duration:</b> Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms:</b> Throne Shadow Form<br /> <br /> The world of the Exalted is a world of vast, eye-catching luminaries; nobody notices a shadow lost in the tangle of the crowd. With Shadow Lost in Court, the martial artist may supplement an ability to establish surprise within a crowd (defined as a scene in which at least 20 characters are present); she may attempt to do so without penalty, and imposes a penalty equal to the number of shadow fingers she has within Close range on attempts to detect her.<br /> <b>Terrestrial</b>: The martial artist does not impose a penalty on those attempting to detect her from her shadow fingers.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:purple\"><b><i>Welcome the Uninvited Guest</i></b></span><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 3m; <b>Mins:</b> Martial Arts (Throne Shadow Style) 5, Essence 2<br /> <b>Type:</b> Simple<br /> <b>Keywords:</b> None<br /> <b>Duration:</b> Five turns<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms:</b> Clear Eyes Defense, Shadow Lost in Court<br /> <br /> Striking the air with her palm, the Sidereal sets an Essence-vibration racing through the world. The martial artist rolls (Perception + Martial Arts); all hidden characters within Short range must make a reflexive opposed (Dexterity + Stealth) roll to remain concealed. All dematerialized beings, and anyone in stealth who fails the opposed roll, become visible as a series of ripples and distortions in the air, losing the benefits of concealment and becoming unable to hide again until five turns have elapsed. <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:purple\"><b><i>Pneuma-Sealing Strike</i></b></span><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 5m; <b>Mins:</b> Martial Arts (Throne Shadow Style) 5, Essence 3<br /> <b>Type:</b> Supplemental<br /> <b>Keywords:</b> Decisive-only, Mastery<br /> <b>Duration:</b> Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms:</b> Throne Shadow Form<br /> <br /> Sidereals are known for their discretion, never sullying the courts of the Lawgivers with the blood of would-be assassins or the screams of intercepted fanatics; their killing arts are cleaner than that. This Charm supplements a grapple gambit, allowing the martial artist to use her weapon's accuracy on the attack roll. If successful, the victim begin to choke as invisible hands squeeze his throat closed; he is unable to cry out or make any vocal noise. The martial artist may only chose to savage or release a victim grappled with Pneuma-Sealing Strike.<br /> <b>Mastery</b>: The martial artist may use her victim's breath against him; doing so costs an additional point of willpower when activating Pneuma-Sealing Strike. The breath manifests as a translucent dire chain (Exalted p. 595), whipping out to Short range to wrap around the victim's throat, extending the range that the martial artist can begin the grapple. This weapon vanishes one turn after the grapple ends as the victim catches his breath.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:purple\"><b><i>Showing the Secret Hand</i></b></span><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 3m per finger; <b>Mins:</b> Martial Arts (Throne Shadow Style) 5, Essence 3<br /> <b>Type:</b> Reflexive<br /> <b>Keywords:</b> Withering-only, Counterattack<br /> <b>Duration:</b> Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms:</b> Clear Eyes Defense, Pneuma-Sealing Strike<br /> <br /> The Sidereal, having enriched the world with his lessons, has earned its gratitude. The world moves to punish those would attempt to strike down such a wise master. When the martial artist is attacked, she may pay for up to (Essence) shadow fingers to make a withering martial arts counterattack against her attacker. Showing the Secret Hand costs 3 motes per finger activated. If her shadow fingers are in a battle group, they instead will make a normal attack, supplemented by a reflexive order issued by the martial artist using (Charisma + Martial Arts) instead of (War).<br /> Showing the Secret Hand does not confer an ability for the martial artist's shadow fingers to reach an opponent who is out of range. Showing the Secret Hand does not count as the shadow finger's action and cannot be used in response to another counterattack. Individual shadow fingers may opt not to participate in this counterattack at no cost.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:purple\"><b><i>World as Weapon Mastery</i></b></span><br /> <b>Cost:</b> (1wp); <b>Mins:</b> Martial Arts (Throne Shadow Style) 5, Essence 3<br /> <b>Type:</b> Reflexive<br /> <b>Keywords:</b> Mastery<br /> <b>Duration:</b> Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms:</b> Welcome the Uninvited Guest, Showing the Secret Hand<br /> <br /> Those who wield the world as a weapon are never alone, and as such, cannot be defeated. The martial artist may apply her Martial Arts Excellency and any instant duration Throne Shadow Style charm to any shadow finger she can see within Long range, at a one willpower point surcharge. She pays all the normal costs of the charms, and uses her attributes and abilities for determining any dice adding limits. The martial artist may treat herself as a finger of the shadow finger she is enhancing.<br /> <b>Mastery</b>: Once she has paid the willpower to enhance a shadow finger's actions, the martial artist may freely enhance their actions without paying the surcharge again for the remainder of the scene. She still must pay the willpower to enhance the first action of a second finger, and so on.<br /> <br /> ----<br /> <br /> <i>Can Sidereals make custom charms for this style? Do they automatically gain the Mastery effects?</i><br /> <br /> No. Throne Shadow Style is no longer 'Sidereal Hero Style'- it is just another martial art, albiet one dedicated to emulating the practiced motions of the agents of destiny. As such, the Sidereals have no greater affinity for Throne Shadow Style than they do any other- which is to say, they can be very effective at it, but they cannot invent new Charms within the style, nor do they automatically gain the Mastery effects.<br /> <br /> <i>What happened to the charms that got cut?</i><br /> <br /> The Lotus Blossoms was cut because A) it no longer makes sense as part of a martial arts tree rather than 'Sidereal Hero Style', and B) because Divine Transcendence of Martial Arts is no longer a thing.<br /> <br /> Deadliest of All Weapons was cut because it felt out of step from the rest of the style- truth-inducing chakra poison is cool, but has nothing to do with the rest of Throne Shadow.<br /> <br /> Flow-Breaking Strike no longer has an elegant representation within Exalted 3E's system for slowing the opponent down. I toyed with some initiative fuckery tricks, and then decided I would rather just wither them.<br /> <br /> Eyes Toward an Ending was really created under a paradigm where activativating Form type charms was much more dangerous than it is in Exalted 3E; as such, it stuck out as something that was very edge-casey.<br /> <br /> <i>If I don't have an Excellency, can I enhance the dice rolls of my shadow fingers via World As Weapon Mastery</i><br /> <br /> Nope.<br /> <br /> <i>That sucks!</i><br /> <br /> You suck!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My Storyteller Vault releases!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/269728/Sorcerous-Ways-Mystic-Martial-Arts\" target=\"_blank\">Sorcerous Ways: Mystic Martial Arts</a> - Punch people for magic power!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/252892/These-Mean-Streets\" target=\"_blank\">These Mean Streets</a> - Advise and systems for street-level punk-noir Vampire larp","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/169-wastevens","name":"wastevens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar169_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"939"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-31T19:55:45-07:00","id":904665,"title":"","content":"Heh. &quot;Brawling aides&quot;. As in, your aides, who are going to be brawling.<br /> Heh.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>But sexually.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1797-ellis","name":"Ellis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1797_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"535"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-31T19:59:32-07:00","id":904666,"title":"","content":"Sexy, this is what I've been waiting for.<br /> <br /> My only question is in Sifu's useful fingers I can assume you can strengthen the intimacy it grants. How does that work if others try to remove it? Is it supernaturally enforced? How can a person who has the intimacy remove it so long as the Sidereal has the Essence committed?<br /> <br /> In hindsight, I also feel that if you're making a battle group, doing something cool like the form boosting their Drill, Might, or some other special advantage would be neat. In which case the Deadliest of All Weapons could be brought back, as the deadliest weapons are not swords, but your allies.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Read my shit at my <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/271207-sandact6-homebrew-topic\" target=\"_blank\">homebrew</a> topic, 2.5e and 3e material!<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1263020-alchemicals-2-0-3e-conversion-charm-design-request\" target=\"_blank\">Play Alchemical's in 3e now</a>, you're welcome.","edited":{"userid":1183,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1183-sandact6","user":"Sandact6","date":". 05-31-2016, 11:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1183-sandact6","name":"Sandact6","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1183_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1236"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-31T20:09:45-07:00","id":904670,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sandact6</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/904662-sidereals-wfhl-peerless-masters-of-the-martial-arts-throne-shadow-style?p=904666#post904666\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sexy, this is what I've been waiting for.<br /> <br /> My only question is in Sifu's useful fingers I can assume you can strengthen the intimacy it grants. How does that work if others try to remove it? Is it supernaturally enforced? How can a person who has the intimacy remove it so long as the Sidereal has the Essence committed?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wastevens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/904662-sidereals-wfhl-peerless-masters-of-the-martial-arts-throne-shadow-style#post904662\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">so long as the mote remains committed, nothing can completely remove this loyalty</div> </div> </div> </div>If the intimacy is raised in rank via subsequent instill actions, it can increase or decrease normally- but nothing can totally eliminate it.<br /> <br /> I'm open to better ways to phrase that; I don't want it to be 'cannot be weakend' or 'cannot be changed', because it feels like it should be able to be intensified (and subsequently diminished)- but not totally eliminated.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My Storyteller Vault releases!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/269728/Sorcerous-Ways-Mystic-Martial-Arts\" target=\"_blank\">Sorcerous Ways: Mystic Martial Arts</a> - Punch people for magic power!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/252892/These-Mean-Streets\" target=\"_blank\">These Mean Streets</a> - Advise and systems for street-level punk-noir Vampire larp","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/169-wastevens","name":"wastevens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar169_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"939"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-31T20:13:32-07:00","id":904674,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sandact6</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/904662-sidereals-wfhl-peerless-masters-of-the-martial-arts-throne-shadow-style?p=904666#post904666\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In hindsight, I also feel that if you're making a battle group, doing something cool like the form boosting their Drill, Might, or some other special advantage would be neat. In which case the Deadliest of All Weapons could be brought back, as the deadliest weapons are not swords, but your allies.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Form *is* doing something cool with a battle group of shadow fingers- a Sidereal that juices a reflexive order action will probably add around 5 to 7 dice regularly to her battle group finger's attack, on top of them *probably* being an elite cadre of martial artists, and without consuming her own action (or she can rally- again, without giving up her own action). Fear and pity the anathema who faces a Sidereal's train shikari death squad!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My Storyteller Vault releases!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/269728/Sorcerous-Ways-Mystic-Martial-Arts\" target=\"_blank\">Sorcerous Ways: Mystic Martial Arts</a> - Punch people for magic power!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/252892/These-Mean-Streets\" target=\"_blank\">These Mean Streets</a> - Advise and systems for street-level punk-noir Vampire larp","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/169-wastevens","name":"wastevens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar169_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"939"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-01T07:10:50-07:00","id":904940,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wastevens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/904662-sidereals-wfhl-peerless-masters-of-the-martial-arts-throne-shadow-style#post904662\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <i>Can Sidereals make custom charms for this style? Do they automatically gain the Mastery effects?</i><br /> <br /> No. Throne Shadow Style is no longer 'Sidereal Hero Style'- it is just another martial art, albiet one dedicated to emulating the practiced motions of the agents of destiny. As such, the Sidereals have no greater affinity for Throne Shadow Style than they do any other- which is to say, they can be very effective at it, but they cannot invent new Charms within the style, nor do they automatically gain the Mastery effects.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I'm going to disagree with this part. Sidereals should have greater affinity for Violet Biers of Sorrows and Throne Shadow Style. Dragonblooded have Immaculate Arts without a Mastery Keyword. Maybe Throne Shadow should not have a Mastery but have a Sidereal Keyword? Of course, the topic of Solars not being the greatest at every MA has strong opinions on either side.<br /> <br /> I was unaware that you can not create new MA Charms. <br /> <br /> Otherwise the style looks good. Throne Shadow is my favorite MA. I like how the Throne Shadow Artist now has to have a greater MA rating than the Shadow Fingers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-01T07:16:34-07:00","id":904943,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/904662-sidereals-wfhl-peerless-masters-of-the-martial-arts-throne-shadow-style?p=904940#post904940\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm going to disagree with this part. Sidereals should have greater affinity for Violet Biers of Sorrows and Throne Shadow Style. Dragonblooded have Immaculate Arts without a Mastery Keyword. Maybe Throne Shadow should not have a Mastery but have a Sidereal Keyword? Of course, the topic of Solars not being the greatest at every MA has strong opinions on either side.<br /> <br /> I was unaware that you can not create new MA Charms.<br /> <br /> Otherwise the style looks good. Throne Shadow is my favorite MA. I like how the Throne Shadow Artist now has to have a greater MA rating than the Shadow Fingers.</div> </div> </div> </div>Re: Affinity for Violet Biers and Throne Shadow (Mastery vs Sidereal)<br /> <br /> I'll grant you, that is a potentially divisive topic. I'm sticking to the book at the moment, and allowing Sidereals peerless mastery to express itself via ignoring Essence requirements on non Sidereal Martial Arts charms, always favored access to Martial Arts and getting the Martial Arts merit for free, as well as having the ability to gain access to the Mastery effects in their own esoteric ways.<br /> <br /> Re: Making custom martial arts charms<br /> <br /> I mean- alright, I'm inferring / assuming on that front, that martial arts styles are 'closed' as they were in 1E and 2E. I'm not sure I can lay hands on anything that says that explicitly though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My Storyteller Vault releases!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/269728/Sorcerous-Ways-Mystic-Martial-Arts\" target=\"_blank\">Sorcerous Ways: Mystic Martial Arts</a> - Punch people for magic power!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/252892/These-Mean-Streets\" target=\"_blank\">These Mean Streets</a> - Advise and systems for street-level punk-noir Vampire larp","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/169-wastevens","name":"wastevens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar169_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"939"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-01T09:09:08-07:00","id":904995,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wastevens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/904662-sidereals-wfhl-peerless-masters-of-the-martial-arts-throne-shadow-style?p=904943#post904943\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean- alright, I'm inferring / assuming on that front, that martial arts styles are 'closed' as they were in 1E and 2E. I'm not sure I can lay hands on anything that says that explicitly though.</div> </div> </div> </div>Page 426 of the 3rd Edition Core:<br /> &quot;The Charms of a style are organized into a single tree, which can be learned by any of the Exalted (and certain other powerful supernatural beings). As a general rule, the Charm tree of each style is complete, the totality of the style\u2019s teachings that have passed down for generations or more. While characters may experiment with creating new styles, they cannot add additional Charms to existing styles. However, at the Storyteller\u2019s discretion, it may be possible to find lost Charms known only to ancient masters or long-lost repositories of wisdom, or for a character to achieve a new understanding of a style by seeking inspiration from an epic quest or unexpected source.&quot;<br /> <br /> Personally however I think Throne Shadow should be open-ended for Sidereals.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew/rewrites:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/882274-new-spell-and-some-2nd-edition-spells-rewrite-for-3rd-edition-peach\" target=\"_blank\">2nd-&gt;3rd Edition Sorcery Spells Rewrite</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=890192#post890192\" target=\"_blank\">Talisman of Ten Thousand Eyes Evocations</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/913443-occult-sorcery-charms-homebrew-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Solar Occult Charms for Sorcerers</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/903155-peach-solar-thrown-charms-for-different-fighting-style-11-charms\" target=\"_blank\">Solar Thrown Charms (with Solar Danmaku Charms)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11704-daerian","name":"Daerian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11704_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-01T09:34:22-07:00","id":905014,"title":"","content":"I &lt;3 Throne Shadow Style. That said, I feel like Lotus Eye Tactics remains a speedbump. Yes, it allows you to do something that you probably couldn't do without a Charm, but is that thing really worth buying a Charm to do? I'm not sure it is.<br /> <br /> Or perhaps I can put it this way: it's probably worth it if you are playing a kung-fu movie chronicle where everyone does kung fu, but if you're not then it's almost certainly going to be a source of disappointment. It's easy to imagine being a player and using this Charm frequently out of a desire to justify the required purchase, only to be constantly told &quot;no, <i>this </i>desert raider <i>also </i>doesn't know kung fu&quot; and the like. Not really a desirable result. Mandatory pre-Form Charms probably ought not to be quite so niche.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Share your wonders in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop#post823884\" target=\"_blank\">The Artifact and Evocation Workshop</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1315-ferryman","name":"Ferryman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1315_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"960"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-01T09:40:57-07:00","id":905018,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ferryman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/904662-sidereals-wfhl-peerless-masters-of-the-martial-arts-throne-shadow-style?p=905014#post905014\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I &lt;3 Throne Shadow Style. That said, I feel like Lotus Eye Tactics remains a speedbump. Yes, it allows you to do something that you probably couldn't do without a Charm, but is that thing really worth buying a Charm to do? I'm not sure it is.<br /> <br /> Or perhaps I can put it this way: it's probably worth it if you are playing a kung-fu movie chronicle where everyone does kung fu, but if you're not then it's almost certainly going to be a source of disappointment. It's easy to imagine being a player and using this Charm frequently out of a desire to justify the required purchase, only to be constantly told &quot;no, <i>this </i>desert raider <i>also </i>doesn't know kung fu&quot; and the like. Not really a desirable result. Mandatory pre-Form Charms probably ought not to be quite so niche.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mm; I see Lotus Eye Tactics as serving two purposes.<br /> A) Can this minion serve as a potential finger?<br /> B) Is this unassuming servant secretly a ninja assassin?<br /> <br /> I've seen effects like Lotus Eye Tactics used to great effect before- it's niche, but I feel like it serves a useful and valuable niche as opposed to a purely invented one.<br /> <br /> (Ironically, the one piece of feedback I got on Reddit was that LET was too broad in letting you learn too much- makes me more comfortable that it's about in the right place if folks are having opposite reactions <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> )<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My Storyteller Vault releases!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/269728/Sorcerous-Ways-Mystic-Martial-Arts\" target=\"_blank\">Sorcerous Ways: Mystic Martial Arts</a> - Punch people for magic power!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/252892/These-Mean-Streets\" target=\"_blank\">These Mean Streets</a> - Advise and systems for street-level punk-noir Vampire larp","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/169-wastevens","name":"wastevens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar169_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"939"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-01T09:45:46-07:00","id":905021,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Daerian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/904662-sidereals-wfhl-peerless-masters-of-the-martial-arts-throne-shadow-style?p=904995#post904995\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Page 426 of the 3rd Edition Core:<br /> &quot;The Charms of a style are organized into a single tree, which can be learned by any of the Exalted (and certain other powerful supernatural beings). As a general rule, the Charm tree of each style is complete, the totality of the style\u2019s teachings that have passed down for generations or more. While characters may experiment with creating new styles, they cannot add additional Charms to existing styles. However, at the Storyteller\u2019s discretion, it may be possible to find lost Charms known only to ancient masters or long-lost repositories of wisdom, or for a character to achieve a new understanding of a style by seeking inspiration from an epic quest or unexpected source.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Danke!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Daerian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/904662-sidereals-wfhl-peerless-masters-of-the-martial-arts-throne-shadow-style?p=904995#post904995\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally however I think Throne Shadow should be open-ended for Sidereals.</div> </div> </div> </div>Eeeh. Agree to disagree- or, at the least, push to 'Throne Shadow is not privileged in the ability for Sidereals to improvise and improve it, although they may have a greater facility in general than other Exalt types.'<br /> <br /> (Hm. That actually gives me a thought for semi-secret arts; Martial Arts charms that are not part of the trees per se, but which Sidereals have retained and passed down from generation to generation- especially charms that require knowledge of two or more styles. I'm definitely going to do Crystal Chameleon Style next, but after that I might focus on those kinds of custom enhancements. Could be an interesting space to explore)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My Storyteller Vault releases!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/269728/Sorcerous-Ways-Mystic-Martial-Arts\" target=\"_blank\">Sorcerous Ways: Mystic Martial Arts</a> - Punch people for magic power!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/252892/These-Mean-Streets\" target=\"_blank\">These Mean Streets</a> - Advise and systems for street-level punk-noir Vampire larp","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/169-wastevens","name":"wastevens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar169_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"939"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-01T10:23:44-07:00","id":905040,"title":"","content":"So if a Solar enhances a Sidereal shadow finger's attack with the capstone + MA Excellency, does the attack have (Dex+MA) or (Essence) as dice-cap ? Can the Sid use charms from other Style to supplement her attack ?<br /> <br /> And are there any reasons you remove the &quot;Fingers counts as a crowd&quot; from Ex2 Shadow Lost In the Court ? The Ex3 version just seems kinda weak now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-01T10:37:33-07:00","id":905047,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/904662-sidereals-wfhl-peerless-masters-of-the-martial-arts-throne-shadow-style?p=905040#post905040\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So if a Solar enhances a Sidereal shadow finger's attack with the capstone + MA Excellency, does the attack have (Dex+MA) or (Essence) as dice-cap ? Can the Sid use charms from other Style to supplement her attack ?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Solar uses her attributes and abilities for determining the dice caps. So, Solar Sally with Essence 4, Dexterity 5 and Martial Arts 5 has a finger of Sidereal Sid, with Essence 2, Dexterity 3 and Martial Arts 1.<br /> <br /> Sid is fighting a gribbling thing as a part of a training exercise! Sally uses World as Weapon Mastery to enhance Bu's attack with 10 dice via Excellency. This is explicitly allowed to exceed Sid's normal dice cap. Sid *can* still use the Fateful Excellency's ability to reduce target numbers, because that operates independent of the dice cap.<br /> <br /> Next turn, the thing is still standing, but Sal wants to back off her help. She only adds 1 die to Sid's attack; Sid can now use the Fateful Excellency to add 1 more die (hitting his dice cap), and then reduce the TN.<br /> <br /> (Hm. That's not as clear as I'd like... have to think of a better way to phrase to make it clear)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/904662-sidereals-wfhl-peerless-masters-of-the-martial-arts-throne-shadow-style?p=905040#post905040\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And are there any reasons you remove the &quot;Fingers counts as a crowd&quot; from Ex2 Shadow Lost In the Court ? The Ex3 version just seems kinda weak now.</div> </div> </div> </div>Kind of personal preference, to be honest. I knocked off the willpower cost (because it felt like it should be a repeatable trick) and gave a stacking non-charm bonus for having shadow fingers nearby (because I like carrots); between those buffs and the disconnect of being able to pull off the Assassin's Creed 'blend into the crowd' thing- with only two good friends being the crowd you blend into.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My Storyteller Vault releases!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/269728/Sorcerous-Ways-Mystic-Martial-Arts\" target=\"_blank\">Sorcerous Ways: Mystic Martial Arts</a> - Punch people for magic power!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/252892/These-Mean-Streets\" target=\"_blank\">These Mean Streets</a> - Advise and systems for street-level punk-noir Vampire larp","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/169-wastevens","name":"wastevens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar169_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"939"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-05T06:43:37-07:00","id":907599,"title":"","content":"I actually *like* this version of Throne Shadow, so cool. I wouldn't want it to be an open style, because of how much that would tag it as too much of a must buy, even for Sidereal players who don't find it particularly in theme for their character's MO, which was one of the big dislikes I always had with the old version from 2e. I could see having a open ended repurchase Charm in there for Sidereals, at most, I think, but it's fine as is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-05T07:50:15-07:00","id":907634,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/904662-sidereals-wfhl-peerless-masters-of-the-martial-arts-throne-shadow-style?p=907599#post907599\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I actually *like* this version of Throne Shadow, so cool. I wouldn't want it to be an open style, because of how much that would tag it as too much of a must buy, even for Sidereal players who don't find it particularly in theme for their character's MO, which was one of the big dislikes I always had with the old version from 2e. I could see having a open ended repurchase Charm in there for Sidereals, at most, I think, but it's fine as is.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Glad to hear it <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My Storyteller Vault releases!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/269728/Sorcerous-Ways-Mystic-Martial-Arts\" target=\"_blank\">Sorcerous Ways: Mystic Martial Arts</a> - Punch people for magic power!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/252892/These-Mean-Streets\" target=\"_blank\">These Mean Streets</a> - Advise and systems for street-level punk-noir Vampire larp","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/169-wastevens","name":"wastevens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar169_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"939"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}